                <pb facs="0323" n="1413" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v06p2/pg1413"/>

                <head>No. 635<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>For extensive documentation on the Geneva Conference, April 26–July 21, 1954,
                    which was largely concerned with matters relating to Korea and Indochina, see
                        <ref target="frus:frus1952-54v16">volume XVI</ref>. The documentation
                    presented in that volume includes exchanges of correspondence between President
                        Eisenhower and President
                        Coty, and between Secretary
                        Dulles and Foreign Minister
                        Bidault, as well as records of
                    numerous United States-French meetings concerning the outcome of the
                    negotiations which took place during both the formal and informal meetings at
                    the Geneva Conference.</p>
            </div>
